🚀 Top 30 Streams, Lambda & Functional Programming Interview Questions
1. What is a Lambda Expression?
(a,b) -> a+b


Answer: A lambda expression is an anonymous function introduced in Java 8 that allows behavior to be passed as data.

2. Why were Lambda Expressions introduced?

✅ Reduce boilerplate code

✅ Functional programming support

✅ Cleaner collections processing

3. What is a Functional Interface?
@FunctionalInterface
interface Calculator {
    int calculate(int a,int b);
}


A functional interface contains exactly one abstract method.

4. Is @FunctionalInterface mandatory?

Answer: No.

It is optional but recommended.

5. Name Four Built-in Functional Interfaces.
Predicate
Function
Consumer
Supplier


Memory Trick:

P-F-C-S

Predicate -> Test
Function  -> Transform
Consumer  -> Consume
Supplier  -> Supply

6. What is Predicate?
Predicate<Integer> even =
    n -> n % 2 == 0;


Used for testing conditions.

Method:

test()

7. What is Function<T,R>?
Function<String,Integer> length =
    String::length;


Used for transformations.

Method:

apply()

8. What is Consumer?
Consumer<String> print =
    System.out::println;


Consumes data.

Method:

accept()

9. What is Supplier?
Supplier<String> s =
    () -> "Hello";


Provides values.

Method:

get()

